it wouldn't be cyberpunk without  cybernetics  enhancing your body in the cyberpunk  universe is both commonplace but also  incredibly dangerous a slippery slope  where if you deck yourself out too much  you risk losing your humanity but this  was of little concern to one cyborg that  didn't have much humanity back when they  were human  and that's who we're talking about today  the legendary adam smasher  aka the guy who killed johnny silverhand  when it comes to these cyberpunk lore  videos we try and talk about characters  and history  we think might be relevant to the  upcoming video game  adam smasher is no exception and he'll  be making an appearance in 2077  right there so let's take a look at the  brief  but important history of adam smasher  adam real name unknown started out as a  typical street punk  in new york city growing up in the south  bronx adam was the leader  of his neighborhood gang the blood boys  even back then he had a nasty sadistic  streak with a dismissive attitude  towards human life  this would serve him well when he later  joined up with the army  although the army didn't see it the same  way discharging him for  quote bad conduct and insubordination  adam would return to the big apple as a  gun for hire  or street samurai as he likes to call it  this line of work suited him  until around 2015 when one day a  job went south and adam was hit by  several rpga  warheads turning him into a bag of meat  that is not a metaphor his friends  literally shoved the chunky remains of  his body  into a backpack and dragged him back to  new york  and yet adam was not fully dead  a mysterious corporation put him on life  support as a pile of flesh  only able to communicate through a tech  interface  they gave him an offer he could be saved  fully converted into a metal body  in exchange for 15 years of service to  them  adam accepted edwan's reborn as the  combat cyborg  adam smasher this mysterious employer  turned out to be  none other than the arasaka corporation  adam smasher became one of their prized  killers while still given the freedom to  work freelance  he would take on any job so long as it  fulfilled one condition  it needed to involve collateral damage  and civilian casualties  adam has long been obsessed with the  idea of being the strongest and  considered himself superior with his  metal body  adopting the mantra metal is better than  meat  his need to prove his way of life led to  a rivalry with the famous solo  morgan blackhand morgan was the opposite  of adam in almost every way  a professional that handled delicate  situations with grace  taking his targets in alive if possible  if adam could beat morgan he could prove  that metal was in fact better than meat  however  every time adam challenged him morgan  would ignore it  eventually the fourth corporate war  kicked off a bloody conflict between  arasaka and militech adam was called in  working the front lines for arasaka all  the while waiting for his chance to take  on morgan  who just so happened to be working for  militech he finally got his wish during  the infamous attack on the night city  arasaka tower  the details of this event are vague a  mystery to the general public of the  cyberpunk universe  and books like cyberpunk red state that  no one really knows what went down  however the adventure book shock wave  not only details what happened  but lets players participate in the  event what i'm about to talk about  is canonically supposed to have happened  but it's worth keeping in mind that  cyberpunk 2077  might change some of the details looking  to end the war  militech sent several strike teams into  arasaka tower  one led by morgan and another led by  rocker boy  johnny silverhand johnny's team was  tasked with breaking into the soulkiller  lab  which housed a dangerous program that  trapped people's minds in a digital  prison  leaving their body an empty shell the  plan went well  but johnny's team took a little too long  and on their way out  they were confronted by adam smasher and  a group of arasaka soldiers  pinned down in a cramped hallway by  gunfire things were not looking good  knowing their situation was hopeless  johnny smg in hand  tried to buy his team some time by  taking on adam smasher  but against adam's metal shell there  really wasn't much johnny could do  adam pulled out his auto shotgun and  tore johnny's body  into pieces in a matter of mere seconds  the body of the legendary rocker boy hit  the ground  johnny was dead this sacrifice gave  johnny's team  the chance to escape meanwhile morgan  blackhand's team had set up a nuclear  device  inside the building and then began  extraction on the rooftop  but of course it wasn't going to be that  simple adam smasher appeared holding the  mangled remains of one of morgan's  friends while taunting him  over the death of johnny morgan couldn't  ignore adam this time and stayed behind  so the rest of his team could escape  there on the rooftop of arasaka tower  adam smasher finally got his duel  with morgan blackhand a chance to see if  metal  was better than meat morgan's team  watched the battle from the sky  the two were still fighting each other  even as the nuclear detonation destroyed  the tower  under their feet both rivals fell into  the chaos below  their fate left unknown but as we now  know  adam smasher did in fact survive we  don't know much about what he's been up  to in the last 50 years but he still  works for arasaka  and has made night city his home which  brings us to cyberpunk 2077  though it hasn't been confirmed i think  it's safe to say he's not going to be an  ally to protagonist v  in fact with v on the run from arasaka  after stealing their prototype chip  i'm hoping adam's role is not unlike a  cyborg version of  resident evil's nemesis a metal  monstrosity  constantly hunting v down v also has the  digital ghost of  johnny silverhand in their head who i'm  sure will want some payback for their  untimely death  perhaps we'll finally get our answer if  metal is better than meat  thank you so much for watching this  episode in our cyberpunk lore series  if you're new i highly recommend you  check out the rest of our videos  such as the one on johnny silverhand and  the fourth corporate war  both of which provide more information  on the events of the destruction of  arasaka tower  we have a new video up every saturday  leading up to cyberpunk 2077's release  so we'll see you next week  you
 

